This product is a static reimplementation inspired by and derived in concept from
Meme Search (https://github.com/meme-search/meme-search), Copyright neonwatty and
contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The example images in memes/classics/ are taken from the Meme Search repository
(meme_search/memes/example_memes_*).

Search results are fetched at runtime, directly by the user's browser, from public
APIs of third parties: Lemmy instances (lemmy.world and others), meme-api.com (Reddit),
api.imgflip.com, en.wikipedia.org, suggestqueries.google.com and, when the user adds
their own API keys, Tenor, Giphy and Imgur. Memegle does not host or redistribute that
content; every result links to its source.

In-browser AI runs on Transformers.js (Apache-2.0) with the models
onnx-community/Florence-2-base-ft, onnx-community/Florence-2-large-ft (MIT, Microsoft)
and Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (Apache-2.0), downloaded from the Hugging Face Hub at runtime.
